--TEST--
a declaration names what it declares and a position names what may stand in it, so `implements` is an interface where `extends` would be a class and `$u->greet()` is a method where `$this->name` is a property, `rule:ide/semantic-tokens-carry-the-qualifiers`, `rule:ide/the-rendering-has-one-home`
--FILE--
<?nvs
namespace App;
interface Greets {
    public function greet(): string;
}
class User implements Greets {
    public string $name;
    public function greet(): string {
        return "hi, " . $this->name;
    }
}
var $u = new User();
echo $u->greet();
--REQUEST--
semanticTokens
--EXPECT--
2:11+3 namespace
3:11+6 interface
4:21+5 method
6:7+4 class
6:23+6 interface
7:19+5 property
8:21+5 method
9:25+5 variable
9:32+4 property
12:5+2 variable
12:14+4 class
13:6+2 variable
13:10+5 method
